258
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,553
Another one?

259
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,306
THE THIRD EMPLOYEE HAS ARRIVED

260
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:47,349
- Hello.
- Hello.

261
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:52,021
Hello.

262
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,439
Nice to meet you. Hello.

263
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:55,524
I'm Kazuha of LE SSERAFIM.

264
00:12:57,026 --> 00:13:01,614
KAZUHA OF GLOBAL GIRL GROUP LE SSERAFIM

265
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:05,284
Who?

266
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:06,619
You don't know me?

267
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:07,745
I've never met her.

268
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:09,079
HE DOESN'T KNOW KAZUHA?

269
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,080
LE SSERAFIM.

270
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:11,248
We've met before.

271
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:13,125
- We have?
- Yes, we have.

272
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:14,793
THEY HAVE MET BEFORE?

273
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,505
- Our song, "Eve, Psyche."
- Okay.

274
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:20,382
You filmed the challenge with us
at our company building.

275
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,801
THEY MET
THROUGH LE SSERAFIM'S SONG CHALLENGE

276
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:23,802
I remember now!

277
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,179
- You remember?
- Yes.

278
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,056
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

279
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,307
I didn't remember either.

280
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:31,644
Both of you didn't remember.

281
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:33,229
I remembered it recently.

282
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,147
- This is nice.
- Please sit.

283
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,440
So we're the members.

284
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:39,443
- Great.
- Hello.

285
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,403
FINALLY, ALL OF THE EMPLOYEES ARE HERE

286
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:43,447
- You're from Japan, right?
- Yes, I am.

287
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:44,990
Your Korean's so good.

288
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,116
Thank you.

289
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:47,910
You speak Japanese, right?

290
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:50,079
- I worked there a bit, so…
- Exactly.

291
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,664
- Right.
- Just a little bit.

292
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:53,832
- Can you speak it?
- You too, right?

293
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:55,960
I started learning recently.

294
00:13:56,043 --> 00:13:57,336
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

295
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:59,630
So we can communicate in Japanese.

296
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,591
TODAY

297
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:04,802
IS OUR

298
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:05,970
Yes.

299
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,806
- And what?
- Beginning.

300
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:09,890
Beginning?

301
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,225
IT'S THE BEGINNING

302
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:12,977
- You're really learning?
- Yes.

303
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,105
I also played in Japan.

304
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:17,648
Right, as a volleyball player.

305
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:19,400
Yes, for two years.

306
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:23,654
- So I can have casual conversations.
- Oh, really?

307
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,364
- Just basics.
- Oh, really?

308
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:29,535
We won't be climbing this time, right?

309
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:30,953
No, we won't.

310
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:32,413
Or sleeping outside?

311
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:33,330
No.

312
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,874
What about the fireplace?

313
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:36,500
The fireplace? It almost killed me.

314
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,294
WORRIED AFTER WATCHING SEASON 1

315
00:14:39,336 --> 00:14:40,170
Are you curious?

316
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:41,881
You prepared something.

317
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,757
I'll brief you now.

318
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,259
BRIEFING ON KIAN'S 2ND B&B

319
00:14:45,342 --> 00:14:47,052
CURIOUS

320
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:49,722
BOSS GETS READY FOR A BRIEFING

321
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:51,724
I'm curious about the house.

322
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:53,058
I'm excited but…

323
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:55,019
- Also worried.
- Please.

324
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:58,063
KIAN'S B&B SEASON 2
BRIEFING

325
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:04,236
Gosh, finally.

326
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:07,239
I'm finally doing this
in front of the employees.

327
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,117
I think we began last summer.

328
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:13,203
We've been having meetings for ideas
to prepare for this

329
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:15,539
since then.

330
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,708
- It's a B&B, right?
- Yes.

331
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:18,959
What kind of B&B

332
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:21,211
will touch our guests' hearts

333
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:24,757
and also entertain our viewers?

334
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,717
In my opinion,

335
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,344
there are no hopes or dreams.

336
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,262
The world is so cruel.

337
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,430
So cold.

338
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:35,851
So I'm hoping our B&B
will be full of hopes and dreams.

339
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:38,687
I'll show you what it looks like first.

340
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:42,149
KIAN'S 2ND B&B, FULL OF HOPE AND DREAMS
WHAT DOES IT LOOK LIKE?

341
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,067
It looks like…

342
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:45,611
KIAN'S B&B

343
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,947
This is the B&B we'll go to.

344
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:50,616
It looks ordinary.

345
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:51,700
It looks ordinary.

346
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:54,411
AN ORDINARY B&B?

347
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:56,455
Notice anything out of the ordinary?

348
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:57,873
Isn't something odd?

349
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,166
Can you see?

350
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:00,709
It's huge.

351
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,002
What?

352
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:04,296
- First, it's very big.
- How did you know?

353
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:05,506
The cow is so small.

354
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:06,966
You sure are sharp.

355
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:08,884
- Right?
- This is a cow.

356
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:11,095
If a cow looks that small…

357
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,346
The house is big.

358
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:14,807
THE HOUSE IS WAY BIGGER THAN A COW

359
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:15,891
The house…

360
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:17,685
How big is it?

361
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:18,852
How big is it, then?

362
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:20,854
- You see…
- Yes?

363
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,481
Everyone likes a big house.

364
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:23,774
Fifty-nine square meters,

365
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:25,651
or 84 m², 112 m².

366
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:28,612
People strive to move into bigger houses.

367
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,823
They like big land and big houses.

368
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:35,077
I thought we should offer our guests
the largest B&B possible.

369
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,328
That's why

370
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,038
we built a big house.

371
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:39,623
But you don't seem to like it.

372
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:41,417
No.

373
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,544
Jun-ho seems to hate it.

374
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:45,004
I'm admiring your imagination.

375
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,130
You are?

376
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:49,508
- Honestly, I never expected this.
- I never imagined it.

377
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:52,428
Now, how do we open this door
that's so much bigger than a cow?

378
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:53,846
Right.

379
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:55,806
So we really need you, Yeon-koung.

380
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:58,058
A DOOR THAT NEEDS YEON-KOUNG TO OPEN?

381
00:16:58,142 --> 00:17:00,394
PROBABLY YEON-KOUNG?

382
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:01,979
Unbelievable.

383
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,569
Someone needs to ride on her shoulders.

384
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:10,529
That's…

385
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,406
We should keep the door open.

386
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,033
No, it'll be so cold.

387
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:16,160
It'll be about -20°C in Daegwallyeong.

388
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:20,039
Now, let's say we go into the house.

389
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:22,124
What does the inside look like?

390
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,751
WHAT'S INSIDE THE WORLD'S BIGGEST B&B?

391
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,545
Like studios near colleges.

392
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:28,964
It feels youthful. It screams youth.

393
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:31,550
Here it is.

394
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:35,095
Our dream, a big house.

395
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:39,266
This is our B&B.

396
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:40,267
What?

397
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,728
What happened to it?

398
00:17:42,811 --> 00:17:44,229
I think they're all so big.

399
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:46,732
The furniture must be ridiculously big.

400
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:49,359
But we have to climb ropes to go up?

401
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,236
Hold on.

402
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,781
THIS IS HOW BIG IT IS INSIDE

403
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:56,450
You have to climb the string
of the top to go up.

404
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:58,202
That's the only way.

405
00:17:58,285 --> 00:18:00,162
I don't think I can.

406
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,498
We'll be sleeping in those boxes?

407
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:05,084
- The <i>ramyeon</i> boxes are our bedrooms?
- Yes.

408
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:08,253
RAMYEON BOXES ARE THEIR BEDROOMS

409
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:10,214
Single room, double room.

410
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,049
- And this…
- Under the TV.

411
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:14,760
I think four people can sleep here.

412
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:17,054
The fridge can fit three people.

413
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:18,555
In the fridge?

414
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:21,642
EVEN THE FRIDGE IS A BEDROOM

415
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,186
You're so imaginative.

416
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:28,190
It does feel like a house of hopes
and dreams, childlike dreams.

417
00:18:28,273 --> 00:18:30,567
What's important is the kitchen.

418
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:37,074
- It's the kitchen, but they're showering.
- On the sink…

419
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:39,660
We'll use the sink as a jacuzzi.

420
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:42,329
THE SINK WILL BE USED AS A JACUZZI

421
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:46,458
- The sink.
- It's that big?

422
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,293
- Like Season 1…
- Yes?

423
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:51,421
Will we be washing clothes where we swim?

424
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,090
No, we won't.

425
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,716
ACTUALLY, WE WILL

426
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:59,221
It's a jacuzzi,
but we'll do the dishes there?

427
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:00,639
And wash clothes.

428
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:03,642
I don't know.

429
00:19:03,725 --> 00:19:04,810
You don't want to go?

430
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:05,978
No, it's not that.

431
00:19:06,061 --> 00:19:08,355
No, it's not that. I want to go.

432
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,565
You look down.

433
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:10,774
- No.
- You look more down.

434
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:11,942
Guys, don't forget.

435
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,777
- Hopes and dreams.
- Hopes and dreams.

436
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:17,322
That'll be all.
That's the end of the briefing.

437
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,578
I see.

438
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:23,912
You look…

439
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:27,583
Boss's imagination…

440
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:30,460
I'm curious to see
how much of it will be realized.

441
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:35,716
I was surprised by his imagination.

442
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,217
I see.

443
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:42,014
I'm not sure how we're going
to survive there for nine days.

444
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:45,601
I'm quite worried, to be honest.

445
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:46,852
Don't worry about the shape.

446
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:49,021
- Really?
- I will make it delicious. Don't worry.

447
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:50,814
COOKING SKILLFULLY

448
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:52,649
CLEANING SKILLFULLY

449
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:54,610
Say hello. They're all new.

450
00:19:55,777 --> 00:19:57,279
MASTER OF GROUP LIVING

451
00:19:57,362 --> 00:19:59,406
- She's good.
- Thank you.

452
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:00,657
Boss, did you wash up?

453
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,701
You keep asking what I did.

454
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,786
- Did you really wash it?
- I did.

455
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:07,122
- Did you brush your teeth?
- Why do you keep…

456
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:10,292
- Hello.
- Hello.

457
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,377
YOU CAN SEE HER VOLLEYBALL SPIKE

458
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:14,922
AS WELL AS SIMILAR SPIKES

459
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,590
Yeon-koung's cycling.

460
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,884
She's amazing, isn't she?

461
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:21,136
SHE'S IN CHARGE OF VARIOUS WORKOUTS TOO

462
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:24,014
YEON-KOUNG ADAPTS TO KIAN'S B&B PERFECTLY

463
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:25,515
Your opinions or ideas.

464
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:29,061
If you have any suggestions
about how to run the B&B,

465
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:30,854
please share them with me.

466
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,648
I think

467
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:35,067
it should be more convenient

468
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,902
when we enter the B&B.

469
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:38,695
Then there won't be hopes and dreams.

470
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:41,323
Then I have to keep carrying them?

471
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:43,200
- It's the biggest house in the world.
- Yes.

472
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:44,534
We must maintain that vibe.

473
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:45,786
FOR HOPES AND DREAMS

474
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,497
If they enter easily,
the image hopes and dreams disappears,

475
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,666
and they'll leave without them.

476
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:53,168
LET'S NOT FORGET ABOUT HOPES AND DREAMS

477
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,253
When we go up,

478
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:58,548
wouldn't it be better if we could climb
without using our hands?

479
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,550
Then there will be no hopes and dreams.

480
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:04,137
THE PROTECTOR OF HOPES AND DREAMS

481
00:21:04,221 --> 00:21:06,348
Is there no other way?

482
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:07,724
No.

483
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:11,770
- We can't let them lose hopes and dreams.
- Right.

484
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,355
But will they like it?

485
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:15,065
- They will.
- They will.

486
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:17,276
I heard 40,000 teams

487
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:18,735
applied for it.

488
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,489
A TOTAL OF 40,000 TEAMS APPLIED

489
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:26,034
TWICE AS MANY APPLICANTS AS SEASON 1

490
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,160
FAMILIES

491
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,120
COUPLES

492
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:29,913
FOREIGNERS, PEOPLE OF RELIGION

493
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:31,415
MORE DIVERSE APPLICANTS

494
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:34,418
WHAT DO THEY EXPECT
FROM KIAN'S BIZARRE B&B SEASON 2?

495
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:36,962
There's fun in experiencing inconvenience.

496
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:39,881
When I saw the climbing walls,
I wanted to do it so badly.

497
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:42,676
No matter how big it is, we can climb it.

498
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:45,137
There's something romantic
about inconvenience.

499
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:46,763
I hope it gets bitterly cold.

500
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:48,640
Like running the marathon topless.

501
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:51,018
EXTREME COLD THAT WILL TEST THEIR LIMITS

502
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:52,352
Since it's Daegwallyeong…

503
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:54,479
I want to scoop the snow and eat it.

504
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:57,065
Maybe make <i>ramyeon</i> with snow?

505
00:21:57,149 --> 00:21:59,109
Make an igloo and sleep in it.

506
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:02,154
It's that sort of dream
of rolling around in the snow.

507
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:05,198
I think youth and romance represent us.

508
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:06,950
ROMANTIC AND YOUTHFUL GUESTS ARE READY

509
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:09,202
I trust you guys

510
00:22:09,286 --> 00:22:11,747
to serve the guests well.

511
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:16,084
One of my regrets from Season 1

512
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,919
was that I noticed the guests

513
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:20,672
wanted to spend more time
with the employees.

514
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:21,715
Oh, really?

515
00:22:22,215 --> 00:22:23,633
But there were some guests

516
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:26,011
I didn't even
get to make eye contact with.

517
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,889
Someone suddenly said they were leaving.

518
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:32,142
I felt so bad.

519
00:22:32,225 --> 00:22:33,685
I was like, "What?"

520
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:35,187
I still feel bad.

521
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:37,898
We should do what they'll enjoy.

522
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,316
THE 2ND B&B PUTS GUESTS FIRST

523
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:42,069
So we'll only provide dinner, right?

524
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:43,361
Yes, just one meal per day.

525
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,572
Are you two good at cooking?

526
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:46,698
Just basic dishes.

527
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:49,993
I used to live alone
while studying abroad.

528
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:52,454
So I think I can cook with recipes.

529
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:55,290
Me too. If I have a recipe,
I can cook it by myself.

530
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:56,458
Just that much.

531
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,043
We should prepare one each.

532
00:22:58,126 --> 00:23:00,003
I think simple dishes will be better.

533
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,296
Like kimchi fried rice.

534
00:23:01,379 --> 00:23:03,048
- It's simple.
- Sounds good.

535
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:05,509
I'm from Osaka,
and <i>okonomiyaki</i> is good too.

536
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,636
<i>Okonomiyaki?</i> This?

537
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:09,387
- Like pancakes?
- Yes.

538
00:23:09,471 --> 00:23:11,556
JUN-HO WILL PREPARE ONE TOO

539
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,477
Anyway, nice meeting you.

540
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,895
Let's do our best.

541
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:18,355
Sure. I look forward to it.

542
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:20,148
- Me too.
- We have a month left.

543
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:21,691
- A month left now.
- A month.

544
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:22,692
Let's do it.

545
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:25,112
We should make a group chat.

546
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:26,905
- Please make one.
- Give me your number.

547
00:23:27,405 --> 00:23:28,615
Can I have your number?

548
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:30,617
I won't contact you privately.

549
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:33,912
Okay.

550
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:36,665
- Make a group chat.
- Right.

551
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:38,959
THE FIRST MEETING

552
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,629
DAEGWALLYEONG

553
00:23:45,715 --> 00:23:48,552
A POPULAR TRAVEL DESTINATION
AMONG YOUNG PEOPLE

554
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:53,807
THERE ARE RANCHES

555
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:56,810
THERE IS WIND

556
00:23:57,936 --> 00:24:00,647
IN DAEGWALLYEONG, THE SNOW KINGDOM

557
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:06,278
KIAN'S BIZARRE B&B OPENS

558
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:09,281
It's so cold in Gangwon. Interesting.

559
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,116
11:00 A.M.
DAEGWALLYEONG VILLAGE REST STOP

560
00:24:15,912 --> 00:24:19,249
NEAT

561
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:21,042
You look cool.

562
00:24:21,126 --> 00:24:22,669
Why are you dressed up?

563
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:26,715
I watched Season 1 again,

564
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:29,009
and I was always wearing the same clothes.

565
00:24:29,092 --> 00:24:30,260
SINCE IT'S THE OPENING

566
00:24:30,343 --> 00:24:32,345
- Do we meet here?
- Yes.

567
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:33,930
THE MEETING POINT

568
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:35,765
Here at last.

569
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,853
Gosh, it's snowing as soon as I'm here.

570
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:42,647
A LIGHT SNOWFALL

571
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:46,735
GROWS HEAVIER TO MARK THE OPENING

572
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:50,447
Gosh, it's so cold.

573
00:24:51,823 --> 00:24:53,033
SNIFFLES

574
00:24:54,784 --> 00:24:56,453
SNIFFLES AGAIN

575
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:02,334
RUMMAGING THROUGH HIS BAG

576
00:25:02,417 --> 00:25:04,753
THE TOWEL FROM SEASON 1

577
00:25:07,797 --> 00:25:09,007
IT GOES BACK INTO THE BAG

578
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:11,343
I've been using it for a year.

579
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,762
For the past year.

580
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:16,765
Whose car is that?

581
00:25:17,265 --> 00:25:20,143
It's a Benz, not a Carnival?

582
00:25:20,227 --> 00:25:21,102
WATCHING CAREFULLY

583
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:22,020
Who is it?

584
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:24,147
Oh, it's Jun-ho.

585
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:28,360
Your good days are over now.

586
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:31,488
There will be no Benz from now on.

587
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,200
- Hello.
- Jun-ho.

588
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:36,409
Hello.

589
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:39,204
- Why are you out in the snow?
- What?

590
00:25:39,287 --> 00:25:40,872
It started to snow when I got here.

591
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:42,791
- Yes, I was surprised too.
- Right?

592
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:44,709
Hey, it's cold. You should button up.

593
00:25:45,335 --> 00:25:47,837
I dressed up a bit
since it's the first day.

594
00:25:47,921 --> 00:25:49,923
Your good days are over.

595
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:52,759
- How have you been?
- What?

596
00:25:52,842 --> 00:25:55,387
- How have you been?
- I've been mentally preparing myself.

597
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:56,554
- Mentally preparing?
- Yes.

598
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:57,889
Why? For what?

599
00:25:57,973 --> 00:26:00,058
It feels like joining the army.

600
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:01,726
How about you?

601
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:05,146
I'm not nervous.
I'm looking forward to it.

602
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:06,856
But I have no clue.

603
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:08,400
I feel the same.

604
00:26:08,483 --> 00:26:10,151
- Come on in.
- Okay.

605
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:12,362
It's freezing.

606
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:14,531
Hello.

607
00:26:14,614 --> 00:26:16,116
- Hello.
- Hi.

608
00:26:16,825 --> 00:26:18,368
- Hello.
- Hello.

609
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:19,369
Sit.

610
00:26:19,452 --> 00:26:20,662
It's snowing a lot.

611
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:22,205
It's freezing.

612
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:24,416
- Are you all right?
- It's warm in Seoul.

613
00:26:26,084 --> 00:26:27,919
- Are you wearing a suit?
- Yes.

614
00:26:28,461 --> 00:26:30,380
- I was going to wear a tie too.
- Yes.

615
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:31,631
But it seemed too much.

616
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:33,633
You look cool today.

617
00:26:33,717 --> 00:26:36,136
We might have to work
as soon as we get there.

618
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:37,220
THE NEW HIRE HAS SPIRIT

619
00:26:37,304 --> 00:26:38,722
- So I'm prepared for that.
- Right.

620
00:26:38,805 --> 00:26:40,807
It's because it's our first day.

621
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:43,101
We won't even
think about our clothes there.

622
00:26:43,184 --> 00:26:44,227
Let's enjoy it today.

623
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:46,021
LOOKING COOL IN EXCHANGE FOR FEELING COLD

624
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:47,355
- Are you okay?
- It's so cold.

625
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,815
- She's here.
- I couldn't sleep.

626
00:26:48,898 --> 00:26:49,733
- Really?
- Yes.

627
00:26:49,816 --> 00:26:51,359
- Zuha's here.
- Hello.

628
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,195
WITH ZUHA ARRIVING LAST

629
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:55,613
- Hello.
- Hello.

630
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,240
EVERYONE'S GATHERED

631
00:26:57,324 --> 00:26:59,034
It feels strange.

632
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,535
- Are you feeling good?
- Yes, I am.

633
00:27:00,618 --> 00:27:02,912
Okay, then shall we head out?

634
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:04,497
- Shall we?
- Let's go.

635
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:05,582
THEY LEAVE FOR THE B&B

636
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:07,417
- Who will drive?
- I will.

637
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:10,045
JUN-HO IS THE DRIVER

638
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:13,923
It's so spacious.

639
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:16,051
RIDING IN THE COMPANY CAR

640
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:17,344
Zuha, do you have leg space?

641
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:18,595
Yes, it's good.

642
00:27:18,678 --> 00:27:20,555
LEAVING FOR KIAN'S B&B
THAT'S 15 MINUTES AWAY

643
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:23,892
By the way,
Jun-ho messaged us a few days ago.

644
00:27:23,975 --> 00:27:24,893
Right.

645
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:27,062
- To wish you a Happy New Year.
- Gosh.

646
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:29,064
I didn't expect
the chat would be so quiet.

647
00:27:29,147 --> 00:27:29,981
Really?

648
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:32,233
I thought you'd say something.

649
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:35,028
I mean, you're the boss.

650
00:27:35,111 --> 00:27:37,322
I'm not the type to reach out first.

651
00:27:37,405 --> 00:27:39,240
You should look after your employees.

652
00:27:39,324 --> 00:27:41,493
- Yes, you should.
- I felt so awkward.

653
00:27:41,576 --> 00:27:43,536
THE BOSS IS TOO SHY

654
00:27:43,620 --> 00:27:45,288
How do you feel now?

655
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,206
- Me?
- Yes.

656
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:48,249
I think I feel a bit shy.

657
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:49,292
Shy?

658
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:51,044
- You feel awkward?
- A bit.

659
00:27:51,127 --> 00:27:53,296
So do I. I feel awkward.

660
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,757
Can I talk casually to you?

661
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:56,674
Yes, totally.

662
00:27:56,758 --> 00:27:59,177
- Let's all talk casually.
- Yes, let's.

663
00:27:59,260 --> 00:28:00,762
- "Hey, Jun-ho." Like this?
- Yes.

664
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:01,679
That's good.

665
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:03,264
I'll talk casually to Zuha.

666
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:05,183
And you to me, Yeon-koung.

667
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:08,436
I mean, I think this is
such an unexpected combination.

668
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:11,481
Anyway, I hope we all get along well.

669
00:28:11,564 --> 00:28:12,690
I hope so too.

670
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:14,192
DEEP INTO THE MOUNTAINS THEY GO

671
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:15,360
We're almost there.

672
00:28:16,736 --> 00:28:18,780
- We're here.
- What?

673
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:20,156
What's that?

674
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,825
Did you draw that?

675
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:23,451
Over there.

676
00:28:23,535 --> 00:28:25,120
THEY ARRIVE AT THE ENTRANCE

677
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:26,746
We should be careful here.

678
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:31,876
KIAN'S B&B

679
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:33,628
It's beginning now.

680
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:36,214
But the road looks…

681
00:28:36,297 --> 00:28:37,966
Where are we going?

682
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:39,968
It's quite a long way from here.

683
00:28:40,051 --> 00:28:41,136
Really?

684
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:42,429
A SINGLE ROAD IN FRONT OF THEM

685
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:43,972
Let's go carefully.

686
00:28:44,055 --> 00:28:46,641
- From this point on, it's not on the map.
- I know.

687
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:48,601
It's not in the GPS.

688
00:28:48,685 --> 00:28:50,937
Can the guests even come here?

689
00:28:51,020 --> 00:28:54,983
Or is it too far to walk from here?

690
00:28:55,066 --> 00:28:56,901
Yes, it's too far.

691
00:28:56,985 --> 00:28:57,819
Is that so?

692
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:01,239
It won't be easy to come here.

693
00:29:05,076 --> 00:29:07,996
How are the guests supposed to come here?

694
00:29:08,079 --> 00:29:09,414
It's so far.

695
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:11,291
This is absurd, Kazuha.

696
00:29:11,374 --> 00:29:13,960
- It's there. I can see it.
- It's there.

697
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:17,213
I can see the B&B.

698
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:19,883
- That's it?
- That's it?

699
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:21,968
- That's it?
- That's it?

700
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:24,095
That must be it.

701
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:26,347
- This is crazy.
- That's it?

702
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:30,769
A HOUSE CAN BE SEEN IN THE DISTANCE

703
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:33,313
- But it's not that big.
- Right.

704
00:29:33,396 --> 00:29:35,023
- Didn't you say it was huge?
- Is it?

705
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:37,400
It's because it's far away.

706
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:39,527
- Really?
- It's big up close?

707
00:29:39,611 --> 00:29:41,029
Once you're close…

708
00:29:41,988 --> 00:29:43,114
It's really big?

709
00:29:44,991 --> 00:29:46,576
Let's bring our stuff now.

710
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:48,119
THEY ARRIVE AT THE PARKING LOT

711
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:52,957
PARKING LOT, KIAN'S B&B

712
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:56,795
- Be careful.
- Okay.

713
00:29:56,878 --> 00:29:59,088
- Be careful, Zuha. Need help?
- Okay.

714
00:29:59,172 --> 00:30:01,591
THEY WALK DOWN THE PATH TO THE B&B

715
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:04,427
Follow the footprints, or you'll slip.

716
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:12,936
This feels so strange.
It looks like an illusion.

717
00:30:16,689 --> 00:30:19,067
- Hey, the house is getting bigger.
- What?

718
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,568
- It is.
- Yes.

719
00:30:21,611 --> 00:30:24,364
The house is getting bigger!

720
00:30:26,324 --> 00:30:28,076
It's getting bigger!

721
00:30:29,118 --> 00:30:29,994
It's so big.

722
00:30:32,539 --> 00:30:34,874
How did they build this?

723
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:42,340
Hey, the door really is huge.

724
00:30:42,423 --> 00:30:45,510
- We really need to get on your shoulders.
- I know!

725
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:48,096
<i>Actually, when they see this,</i>

726
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:51,182
I hope they think it's nothing special.

727
00:30:51,766 --> 00:30:53,768
<i>See this cow next to it?</i>

728
00:30:55,395 --> 00:30:57,397
<i>It's not a dog, it's a cow.</i>

729
00:30:58,314 --> 00:30:59,858
IT LOOKS LIKE AN ORDINARY HOUSE

730
00:30:59,941 --> 00:31:02,318
<i>"Wait, something's not right."</i>

731
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:06,239
<i>The closer you get, the bigger it gets.</i>

732
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:08,408
<i>That's how this house looks from outside.</i>

733
00:31:08,908 --> 00:31:12,287
AT THE FOOT OF DAEGWALLYEONG
1,000 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

734
00:31:13,121 --> 00:31:15,623
THE HOUSE OF HOPES AND DREAMS STANDS ALONE

735
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:22,714
KIAN'S SECOND IMAGINATION
HAS BECOME REALITY HERE

736
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:25,425
Goodness, the door's huge!

737
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:26,843
It really is huge.

738
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:29,053
- Wait.
- It's amazing.

739
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:30,930
- It's huge.
- It's awesome up close.

740
00:31:34,475 --> 00:31:36,311
I really couldn't tell from afar.

741
00:31:37,604 --> 00:31:38,813
What on earth?

742
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:39,898
It's no joke.

743
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:43,985
KIAN'S B&B

744
00:31:44,068 --> 00:31:45,194
It's big.

745
00:31:46,654 --> 00:31:48,072
It's not real, seriously.

746
00:31:50,199 --> 00:31:51,784
This is the door handle?

747
00:31:51,868 --> 00:31:54,746
192-CM-TALL YEON-KOUNG
TRIES TO OPEN THE DOOR

748
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:59,125
- Can you reach it?
- No, I can't.

749
00:32:00,585 --> 00:32:02,211
SO CLOSE

750
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,298
Even she can't reach it.

751
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,967
Hey, how do we do this?

752
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:11,554
I thought the house
would be perfect for me,

753
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:14,974
but when I got here, I realized it wasn't.

754
00:32:15,058 --> 00:32:17,477
IT'S HARD EVEN FOR YEON-KOUNG TO OPEN IT

755
00:32:18,978 --> 00:32:21,314
5 M-HIGH DOOR

756
00:32:21,397 --> 00:32:23,358
ABOUT 2.6 YEON-KOUNGS TALL

757
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:28,404
THIS HUGE DOOR IS THE ONLY ENTRANCE

758
00:32:28,488 --> 00:32:30,531
Can she open it if she jumps?

759
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,450
Hey, how do we do this?

760
00:32:33,409 --> 00:32:35,870
So do we have to open it every day, then?

761
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:37,497
WE HAVE TO OPEN THIS DOOR EVERY DAY?

762
00:32:37,580 --> 00:32:39,624
- If I hang from it…
- Yes.

763
00:32:39,707 --> 00:32:42,001
- You pull it down.
- I just need to pull it down?

764
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:43,753
I think Jun-ho's going to give it a try.

765
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:45,004
ABOUT TO GRAB THE DOOR HANDLE

766
00:32:48,591 --> 00:32:49,884
- Will it work?
- Be careful.

767
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:50,969
HESITATES

768
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:52,220
I don't think I can reach it.

769
00:32:53,137 --> 00:32:54,931
- It's so high.
- Let's go.

770
00:32:58,351 --> 00:32:59,185
But can he…

771
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:03,523
THE DOOR DIDN'T EVEN BUDGE

772
00:33:03,606 --> 00:33:06,192
Hold on.
Just hanging from it doesn't work.

773
00:33:06,275 --> 00:33:08,528
- You have to pull it hard.
- Pull it?

774
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:10,154
How?

775
00:33:10,238 --> 00:33:11,531
Pull it down.

776
00:33:11,614 --> 00:33:13,574
JUST LIKE OPENING A REAL DOOR

777
00:33:20,331 --> 00:33:22,583
I think someone should
get on my shoulders.

778
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:24,836
- Should we do that?
- Yeah.

779
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:26,254
TRIES GETTING ON HIS SHOULDERS

780
00:33:26,337 --> 00:33:29,007
- Will you be okay?
- Or how using a truck and getting on top?

781
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:31,426
- All right.
- One, two, three.

782
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:33,761
One, two, three.

783
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:34,971
Okay.

784
