00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:31,669
But the more convenient they are,
the less memorable.

1040
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:33,754
You already look tired. Are you okay?

1041
00:44:33,837 --> 00:44:35,255
HARDSHIP MAKES MEMORIES

1042
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:39,176
I always do this. I tend to walk
into the trap I made myself.

1043
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:41,595
THE TRAP HE MADE HIMSELF

1044
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:43,555
There's another way there.

1045
00:44:43,639 --> 00:44:45,599
- There is?
- There's a pole.

1046
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,226
I think we can go down here.

1047
00:44:47,309 --> 00:44:48,894
I think so.

1048
00:44:49,603 --> 00:44:52,356
Actually, depending on your preference,

1049
00:44:52,439 --> 00:44:56,026
if you prefer pole climbing,
you can climb the gas pipe.

1050
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:57,069
THE POLE IS BACK

1051
00:44:57,152 --> 00:44:57,986
It's so high.

1052
00:44:58,070 --> 00:44:59,947
4.4 M-HIGH GAS PIPE
ABOUT 2.3 YEON-KOUNGS TALL

1053
00:45:00,030 --> 00:45:01,657
- I can't do it.
- It's scary.

1054
00:45:01,740 --> 00:45:02,699
GIVING UP RIGHT AWAY

1055
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:06,745
God, the ways up and down
are both not easy.

1056
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:07,955
- Like this?
- Yes.

1057
00:45:09,289 --> 00:45:10,499
My feet hurt so much.

1058
00:45:12,501 --> 00:45:14,503
Hey, we have to take them off the hangers.

1059
00:45:14,586 --> 00:45:16,004
- What?
- The clothes.

1060
00:45:16,088 --> 00:45:17,965
- Why?
- They're comforters.

1061
00:45:18,048 --> 00:45:19,508
- They're comforters?
- Yes.

1062
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:21,844
They can use these as comforters.

1063
00:45:21,927 --> 00:45:23,971
But they can also use those.

1064
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:26,056
This is the best stay, I think.

1065
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:27,891
Let's say you crash at a friend's place.

1066
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:29,726
"Hey, want comfy clothes?"

1067
00:45:29,810 --> 00:45:30,894
"Comfy clothes."

1068
00:45:31,645 --> 00:45:33,147
Let's say it's a big T-shirt.

1069
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:36,942
They can use the big T-shirts
as comforters.

1070
00:45:37,025 --> 00:45:37,943
T-SHIRTS
COMFORTERS

1071
00:45:38,569 --> 00:45:40,612
USE A FRIEND'S T-SHIRT AS A COMFORTER

1072
00:45:41,321 --> 00:45:43,907
AND STAY COMFORTABLY
AS IF IT WERE A FRIEND'S PLACE

1073
00:45:44,533 --> 00:45:47,077
FOLD THEM NEATLY AFTER USING THEM

1074
00:45:47,161 --> 00:45:49,496
THERE ARE ALSO HUGE SOCKS

1075
00:45:51,165 --> 00:45:53,959
- How do we get them down?
- How? How do we get up there?

1076
00:45:54,042 --> 00:45:55,961
4 M-HIGH HANGER POLE
ABOUT 2.1 YEON-KOUNGS TALL

1077
00:45:56,044 --> 00:45:57,296
Like a judoka.

1078
00:45:57,379 --> 00:45:59,756
- Climb it.
- We have to climb it?

1079
00:45:59,840 --> 00:46:02,426
Yes, you're on the national team.

1080
00:46:02,509 --> 00:46:05,304
- You're a national athlete.
- I don't train like that.

1081
00:46:05,387 --> 00:46:07,181
Volleyball players don't climb ropes.

1082
00:46:07,264 --> 00:46:08,891
- Don't you all do that?
- No.

1083
00:46:08,974 --> 00:46:10,476
CAN'T YOU DO IT?

1084
00:46:10,559 --> 00:46:12,436
Volleyball players don't climb poles.

1085
00:46:13,061 --> 00:46:14,146
AND IN THE CORNER

1086
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:15,647
What are these boxes?

1087
00:46:15,731 --> 00:46:17,399
Isn't this a room too?

1088
00:46:17,483 --> 00:46:19,151
A SUSPICIOUS RAMYEON BOX

1089
00:46:19,234 --> 00:46:21,069
- It's awesome.
- It's so cute.

1090
00:46:21,153 --> 00:46:23,280
Hey, this is nice. Nice and cozy.

1091
00:46:23,363 --> 00:46:24,740
It's so private.

1092
00:46:24,823 --> 00:46:26,658
Isn't this a solitary cell?

1093
00:46:26,742 --> 00:46:28,076
A PRIVATE ROOM

1094
00:46:28,160 --> 00:46:31,246
What I felt during Season 1 is,

1095
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:35,459
since guests didn't have their own room,
they wanted to rest in a private space.

1096
00:46:36,043 --> 00:46:38,837
Then we should create
some private spaces this time.

1097
00:46:38,921 --> 00:46:40,506
TAKEAWAY FROM 1ST B&B: PERSONAL SPACE

1098
00:46:41,548 --> 00:46:42,716
A <i>ramyeon</i> box?

1099
00:46:44,301 --> 00:46:46,345
Yeah, we need a couple <i>ramyeon</i> boxes.

1100
00:46:47,262 --> 00:46:48,931
One more here.

1101
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:51,975
RAMYEON BOXES:
PRIVATE ROOMS

1102
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:53,685
Hold on. Then…

1103
00:46:53,769 --> 00:46:55,604
This is a room too.

1104
00:46:56,897 --> 00:46:58,941
This is a room too.
I think it's better.

1105
00:46:59,024 --> 00:47:00,359
TOP RAMYEON BOX

1106
00:47:00,442 --> 00:47:02,069
It's open here, so…

1107
00:47:03,070 --> 00:47:04,446
I want to sleep here.

1108
00:47:04,530 --> 00:47:06,156
- You like it?
- Yes.

1109
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:12,287
This one's so nice.

1110
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:14,957
THE TV CABINET IS ALSO A PRIVATE BEDROOM

1111
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:19,336
And the most important thing is the TV.

1112
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:22,548
HOW TO GET TO THE TV
1. CLIMB THE BOX

1113
00:47:22,631 --> 00:47:23,924
How do we climb this one?

1114
00:47:24,925 --> 00:47:26,593
THE ENTRANCE OF THE TV

1115
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:27,844
- How's it?
- Let's go together.

1116
00:47:27,928 --> 00:47:29,513
How do you climb this?

1117
00:47:29,596 --> 00:47:30,722
With bare feet?

1118
00:47:30,806 --> 00:47:31,848
AND…

1119
00:47:34,434 --> 00:47:37,729
HOW TO GET TO THE TV
2. CLIMB THE STRING OF THE TOP

1120
00:47:37,813 --> 00:47:39,690
- Push me up.
- You got it? Give me your hand.

1121
00:47:41,775 --> 00:47:42,693
How is it?

1122
00:47:43,485 --> 00:47:45,821
- You don't want to see?
- I can from here.

1123
00:47:46,863 --> 00:47:47,781
It's great.

1124
00:47:47,864 --> 00:47:49,283
I'm sure you want to see this.

1125
00:47:49,908 --> 00:47:53,495
THEY GO INTO THE TV

1126
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:58,250
You have to see this.

1127
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:00,711
WHAT'S INSIDE THE TV?

1128
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:03,505
Do you see the TV here?

1129
00:48:03,589 --> 00:48:06,258
This adds a nice kick to Kian's B&B.

1130
00:48:06,341 --> 00:48:08,969
The TV screen opens.

1131
00:48:12,347 --> 00:48:13,640
It's a karaoke.

1132
00:48:15,767 --> 00:48:16,935
Wow, that's awesome.

1133
00:48:17,019 --> 00:48:18,770
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

1134
00:48:18,854 --> 00:48:21,231
<i>Inside the TV is like a coin karaoke.</i>

1135
00:48:21,315 --> 00:48:22,316
WELCOME

1136
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:25,986
<i>And when the screen opens,</i>
<i>it becomes a stage.</i>

1137
00:48:26,069 --> 00:48:27,696
AN ORDINARY TV
TRANSFORMS INTO A STAGE

1138
00:48:27,779 --> 00:48:29,823
So I was hoping for singers.

1139
00:48:29,906 --> 00:48:32,075
- And you two came.
- Us?

1140
00:48:33,368 --> 00:48:36,580
YES, YOU GUYS

1141
00:48:44,087 --> 00:48:45,380
- Ta-da.
- Ta-da.

1142
00:48:45,464 --> 00:48:48,592
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE OPENING SOON

1143
00:48:49,259 --> 00:48:51,178
- Isn't it nice?
- Wow.

1144
00:48:51,261 --> 00:48:53,096
- Like this?
- Like this.

1145
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:56,266
If you want to sing in front of people,
you can sing here.

1146
00:48:56,350 --> 00:48:58,226
AUDIENCE SEATING WILL BE AVAILABLE

1147
00:48:58,310 --> 00:48:59,853
You agreed to perform, Kazuha.

1148
00:48:59,936 --> 00:49:01,688
Alone? Let's do it together.

1149
00:49:02,272 --> 00:49:04,691
You singers perform, and so can we.
It's karaoke, after all.

1150
00:49:04,775 --> 00:49:06,109
NO PRESSURE
AT KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

1151
00:49:06,193 --> 00:49:08,445
And I'm sure
some of the guests will sing too.

1152
00:49:08,528 --> 00:49:10,656
- Right.
- They'll want to sing too.

1153
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:12,199
There might be a good singer.

1154
00:49:12,282 --> 00:49:13,825
THEY HAVE FINISHED THE TOUR

1155
00:49:15,369 --> 00:49:20,290
<i>I think 99.9% of it has been realized.</i>
<i>And I find that incredible.</i>

1156
00:49:20,374 --> 00:49:22,042
<i>Wow, did they really make this?</i>

1157
00:49:22,125 --> 00:49:23,960
Oh, this is so nice.

1158
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:25,587
<i>It's great.</i>

1159
00:49:25,671 --> 00:49:29,424
<i>It was amazing, and it was also so fun.</i>

1160
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:31,968
Wow, this is the gym.

1161
00:49:32,761 --> 00:49:35,347
YEON-KOUNG SUGGESTED A GYM BY THE WINDOW

1162
00:49:35,430 --> 00:49:36,807
- An exercise bike?
- Yes.

1163
00:49:36,890 --> 00:49:38,225
<i>Wait, is this a trampoline?</i>

1164
00:49:38,308 --> 00:49:40,644
LAUNDRY BASKET:
TRAMPOLINE

1165
00:49:41,228 --> 00:49:42,479
<i>The bathroom's good enough.</i>

1166
00:49:42,562 --> 00:49:43,730
<i>It's gotten so much better.</i>

1167
00:49:43,814 --> 00:49:45,023
AND THE CABINET BATHROOM

1168
00:49:56,326 --> 00:49:58,453
HOW TO USE THE HUGE TOILET PAPER

1169
00:49:59,121 --> 00:50:00,372
I like the big toilet paper.

1170
00:50:00,914 --> 00:50:02,958
- Isn't this what Zuha suggested?
- Right.

1171
00:50:03,041 --> 00:50:04,000
It's amazing.

1172
00:50:04,835 --> 00:50:07,713
If we could have a skating rink outside…

1173
00:50:07,796 --> 00:50:08,839
- Seriously?
- Yes.

1174
00:50:08,922 --> 00:50:10,674
I think it's good enough.

1175
00:50:11,341 --> 00:50:13,093
- You're good.
- Yes, it's good.

1176
00:50:13,176 --> 00:50:14,177
You're good, Kazuha.

1177
00:50:14,261 --> 00:50:15,846
- It's perfect.
- Yes, it's good.

1178
00:50:15,929 --> 00:50:19,057
AFTER THE TOUR

1179
00:50:20,183 --> 00:50:21,727
Hey, you look so small.

1180
00:50:22,310 --> 00:50:23,478
- Do I?
- Yes.

1181
00:50:24,062 --> 00:50:26,231
You look so <i>kawaii</i> right now.

1182
00:50:26,314 --> 00:50:28,400
KAWAII YEON-KOUNG

1183
00:50:28,483 --> 00:50:30,318
THANK YOU

1184
00:50:31,319 --> 00:50:34,239
THANK YOU, KIAN

1185
00:50:36,742 --> 00:50:38,160
What should we have for dinner?

1186
00:50:38,243 --> 00:50:40,245
- Kimchi fried rice?
- Sounds good.

1187
00:50:40,328 --> 00:50:42,456
Put grilled pork belly
on top of kimchi fried rice?

1188
00:50:42,539 --> 00:50:43,790
Sounds good.

1189
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:46,710
- Then pork belly and kimchi fried rice.
- Okay.

1190
00:50:46,793 --> 00:50:48,211
NEXT, THEY HAVE A MEETING

1191
00:50:48,295 --> 00:50:50,297
Once the guests arrive,
give them comforters.

1192
00:50:50,380 --> 00:50:53,717
And those who have a drink at night,

1193
00:50:53,800 --> 00:50:55,969
ask them to sleep on the first floor.

1194
00:50:56,052 --> 00:50:57,804
And the fridge,

1195
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:59,848
there are safety belts in there.

1196
00:50:59,931 --> 00:51:01,683
Tell them to keep them on.

1197
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:04,227
Those who don't wear belts while sleeping

1198
00:51:04,728 --> 00:51:05,979
will be kicked out.

1199
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:07,063
Kicked out?

1200
00:51:07,647 --> 00:51:08,940
We should keep an eye on them.

1201
00:51:09,024 --> 00:51:10,901
LOOKED AFTER BY THE STAFF

1202
00:51:10,984 --> 00:51:14,154
And we'll turn the lights off at bedtime.

1203
00:51:14,237 --> 00:51:16,948
Should we set it at 11:00 p.m.?

1204
00:51:17,032 --> 00:51:20,368
We have to turn them off,
but they're so high.

1205
00:51:20,452 --> 00:51:21,286
LIGHT SWITCH

1206
00:51:21,369 --> 00:51:23,747
4.7M-HIGH
ABOUT 2.45 YEON-KOUNGS TALL

1207
00:51:23,830 --> 00:51:25,081
Isn't it like training?

1208
00:51:25,165 --> 00:51:27,584
EVEN TURNING OFF THE LIGHTS ISN'T EASY

1209
00:51:27,667 --> 00:51:30,045
- And since it's the first day…
- Yes.

1210
00:51:30,128 --> 00:51:32,255
When the guests are here,

1211
00:51:32,339 --> 00:51:34,424
how about we use the sauna or the jacuzzi?

1212
00:51:34,508 --> 00:51:36,551
- Together?
- Wouldn't it be better?

1213
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:39,221
- Let's decide after dinner, then.
- Okay.

1214
00:51:39,304 --> 00:51:40,555
All together.

1215
00:51:40,639 --> 00:51:42,432
FIRST EVENING EVENT
SAUNA

1216
00:51:42,516 --> 00:51:44,976
Let's decide our rooms first.

1217
00:51:45,060 --> 00:51:46,394
ASSIGNING STAFF ROOMS

1218
00:51:46,478 --> 00:51:48,814
I'm thinking of using the box bedroom.

1219
00:51:48,897 --> 00:51:49,898
- The top box?
- Yes.

1220
00:51:49,981 --> 00:51:52,359
- And Zuha?
- Whichever is fine.

1221
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:55,195
BOTTOM RAMYEON BOX: ZUHA

1222
00:51:55,278 --> 00:51:57,239
TOP RAMYEON BOX: YEON-KOUNG

1223
00:51:57,322 --> 00:51:58,698
Which one will you use?

1224
00:51:58,782 --> 00:51:59,699
Me?

1225
00:52:00,450 --> 00:52:01,785
I like the one under the TV.

1226
00:52:01,868 --> 00:52:03,745
- Then let's use it together.
- Sure.

1227
00:52:03,829 --> 00:52:05,622
TV CABINET: KIAN & JUN-HO

1228
00:52:06,957 --> 00:52:08,124
It's so big.

1229
00:52:09,334 --> 00:52:11,086
BLOWS HIS NOSE

1230
00:52:12,420 --> 00:52:14,089
My forearms are already exhausted.

1231
00:52:15,966 --> 00:52:17,133
- In Season 1…
- Yes.

1232
00:52:17,217 --> 00:52:18,885
I was in great shape when it was over.

1233
00:52:20,554 --> 00:52:21,930
BLOWS HIS NOSE AGAIN

1234
00:52:22,013 --> 00:52:23,515
When did you catch a cold?

1235
00:52:23,598 --> 00:52:24,599
This morning.

1236
00:52:25,100 --> 00:52:25,976
Gosh, it's so cold.

1237
00:52:26,059 --> 00:52:27,727
You shouldn't catch it from me.

1238
00:52:27,811 --> 00:52:29,896
If you catch a cold too, it'll be so bad.

1239
00:52:29,980 --> 00:52:30,897
DON'T CATCH IT FROM ME

1240
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:32,774
- It's okay.
- Still.

1241
00:52:33,775 --> 00:52:36,027
Are you sure
you don't want to switch rooms?

1242
00:52:36,111 --> 00:52:37,028
It's fine.

1243
00:52:38,446 --> 00:52:40,699
Are you sure? I don't mind.

1244
00:52:41,366 --> 00:52:42,200
Are you sure?

1245
00:52:43,827 --> 00:52:44,828
It's fine.

1246
00:52:46,496 --> 00:52:47,414
It's okay.

1247
00:52:48,373 --> 00:52:49,249
AFTER THEY UNPACK

1248
00:52:49,332 --> 00:52:50,375
This is great.

1249
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:52,752
What time is it? It's 12:00 p.m.

1250
00:52:52,836 --> 00:52:54,754
- We haven't even had lunch.
- Right.

1251
00:52:54,838 --> 00:52:57,424
THEY LEAVE TO EAT AND SHOP FOR GROCERIES

1252
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,426
- Did you put on your seat belts? Good.
- Yes.

1253
00:53:00,051 --> 00:53:01,303
Now, let's go.

1254
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:05,015
HEADING DOWNTOWN THAT'S 15 MINUTES AWAY

1255
00:53:05,098 --> 00:53:06,141
They'll like it, right?

1256
00:53:06,224 --> 00:53:07,934
- Like what?
- Our B&B.

1257
00:53:08,935 --> 00:53:11,021
I think they'll be surprised at first.

1258
00:53:11,104 --> 00:53:12,439
It'll feel like a theme park.

1259
00:53:12,522 --> 00:53:13,481
That's right.

1260
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:15,692
What time do they usually call?

1261
00:53:15,775 --> 00:53:16,902
It depends.

1262
00:53:18,778 --> 00:53:20,614
- Some come in the evening.
- Right.

1263
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:21,865
Some come during the day.

1264
00:53:22,824 --> 00:53:24,951
If a lot come from the start,

1265
00:53:25,035 --> 00:53:26,661
- it'll be tough.
- Right.

1266
00:53:26,745 --> 00:53:27,829
MEANWHILE

1267
00:53:28,914 --> 00:53:29,873
It's snowing a lot.

1268
00:53:30,832 --> 00:53:32,167
I'm so excited!

1269
00:53:32,250 --> 00:53:34,085
THE FIRST GUESTS ARRIVE IN PYEONGCHANG

1270
00:53:35,170 --> 00:53:37,505
AND THE STAFF ARRIVE AT THE RESTAURANT

1271
00:53:38,715 --> 00:53:39,841
I'll have the set meal.

1272
00:53:40,425 --> 00:53:42,218
- The set meal?
- There's steamed or grilled.

1273
00:53:42,844 --> 00:53:44,095
Grilled dried pollack.

1274
00:53:44,179 --> 00:53:45,639
I'll have the set meal too.

1275
00:53:45,722 --> 00:53:47,182
Dried pollack soup.

1276
00:53:47,265 --> 00:53:49,434
One soup and three set meals.

1277
00:53:49,517 --> 00:53:51,645
1 DRIED POLLACK SOUP
3 GRILLED DRIED POLLACK SET MEALS

1278
00:53:55,523 --> 00:53:58,193
THE BOSS CAUGHT A COLD TRYING TO LOOK COOL

1279
00:53:59,778 --> 00:54:01,112
HE SPLITS A NEW PIECE OF TISSUE,

1280
00:54:01,196 --> 00:54:02,948
ROLLS THEM,

1281
00:54:03,031 --> 00:54:04,950
AND PUTS THEM

1282
00:54:05,033 --> 00:54:06,576
IN EACH NOSTRIL

1283
00:54:08,036 --> 00:54:10,538
The employees have their own rules.

1284
00:54:11,122 --> 00:54:12,749
RULES FOR EMPLOYEES?

1285
00:54:12,832 --> 00:54:14,834
Well, we set an example.

1286
00:54:15,377 --> 00:54:17,295
We pick up trash as soon as we see it.

1287
00:54:18,129 --> 00:54:20,256
- Whoever sees it first.
- Yes.

1288
00:54:20,924 --> 00:54:22,676
We do the dishes right away.

1289
00:54:22,759 --> 00:54:24,177
Right away.

1290
00:54:24,260 --> 00:54:27,722
I think everyone here
will do it proactively.

1291
00:54:27,806 --> 00:54:30,183
- None of us are irresponsible.
- I'm sure.

1292
00:54:30,266 --> 00:54:31,977
- It looks so good.
- Whose is this?

1293
00:54:32,060 --> 00:54:33,019
GRILLED DRIED POLLACK

1294
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:34,479
We'll share it.

1295
00:54:34,562 --> 00:54:36,481
DRIED POLLACK SOUP

1296
00:54:36,564 --> 00:54:37,816
- Let's share it.
- Enjoy.

1297
00:54:37,899 --> 00:54:38,858
Thank you for the food.

1298
00:54:38,942 --> 00:54:39,943
It's good.

1299
00:54:49,577 --> 00:54:51,162
We have to clean too.

1300
00:54:51,246 --> 00:54:52,163
Of course.

1301
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:53,999
- And dust off the comforters.
- Yes.

1302
00:54:54,082 --> 00:54:56,668
And we have to keep the jacuzzi clean.

1303
00:54:56,751 --> 00:54:58,420
Right. And do the laundry.

1304
00:54:58,503 --> 00:54:59,671
CHECKING THINGS TO DO

1305
00:54:59,754 --> 00:55:01,089
Darn it, the laundry.

1306
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:03,633
- The laundry…
- Hey, the laundry…

1307
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:05,802
Your nose really keeps running.

1308
00:55:05,885 --> 00:55:06,886
The laundry…

1309
00:55:06,970 --> 00:55:09,723
You've got a bad cold. Are you okay?

1310
00:55:09,806 --> 00:55:11,057
What about the hospital?

1311
00:55:11,141 --> 00:55:12,642
- Don't worry.
- That's the spirit.

1312
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:14,394
I want to go to the hospital.

1313
00:55:19,441 --> 00:55:21,526
I'm sorry, but why do I have two cups?

1314
00:55:21,609 --> 00:55:24,070
2 PAPER CUPS IN FRONT OF YEON-KOUNG

1315
00:55:27,115 --> 00:55:29,117
Let's just share them. We'll get closer.

1316
00:55:32,287 --> 00:55:33,830
HATING IT

1317
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:35,373
This is mine.

1318
00:55:35,457 --> 00:55:37,625
- Are you sure?
- Probably.

1319
00:55:41,087 --> 00:55:43,298
THE BOSS'S CUP
YEON-KOUNG'S CUP

1320
00:55:45,508 --> 00:55:47,260
THE CUPS WERE SWITCHED

1321
00:55:47,343 --> 00:55:49,763
THE BOSS'S CUP

1322
00:55:58,813 --> 00:55:59,856
Is the call from a guest?

1323
00:55:59,939 --> 00:56:01,566
I have a feeling it is.

1324
00:56:02,275 --> 00:56:03,151
Is it?

1325
00:56:04,235 --> 00:56:08,490
NERVOUS

1326
00:56:10,658 --> 00:56:11,743
Hello?

1327
00:56:11,826 --> 00:56:13,495
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hi.

1328
00:56:13,578 --> 00:56:16,247
<i>We're guests at Kian's B&B for today.</i>

1329
00:56:16,331 --> 00:56:18,416
- Yes.
<i>- I called you to check in.</i>

1330
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:19,334
I see.

1331
00:56:19,417 --> 00:56:21,419
Where are you right now, then?

1332
00:56:21,503 --> 00:56:24,297
We're at Daegwallyeong Yangtte Ranch.

1333
00:56:24,380 --> 00:56:25,924
Yangtte Ranch?

1334
00:56:26,007 --> 00:56:27,092
ALREADY AT DAEGWALLYEONG

1335
00:56:27,175 --> 00:56:30,136
So you didn't drive here?

1336
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:31,596
<i>We came by taxi.</i>

1337
00:56:31,679 --> 00:56:32,514
By taxi?

1338
00:56:32,597 --> 00:56:35,100
- I'll send you the address.
<i>- Okay.</i>

1339
00:56:35,183 --> 00:56:36,267
Did you drive here?

1340
00:56:36,351 --> 00:56:38,061
ASKING WHAT HE JUST ASKED AGAIN

1341
00:56:38,144 --> 00:56:39,312
- Taxi.
- Taxi.

1342
00:56:39,395 --> 00:56:40,939
Right, taxi.

1343
00:56:41,022 --> 00:56:42,190
Right, taxi.

1344
00:56:42,273 --> 00:56:45,652
We'll send you the address soon.

1345
00:56:45,735 --> 00:56:47,862
COVERING FOR THE BOSS
WHO'S NOT FEELING WELL

1346
00:56:47,946 --> 00:56:50,323
I think you should come
between 3:30 and 4:00 p.m.

1347
00:56:50,406 --> 00:56:51,407
1:45 P.M.

1348
00:56:51,491 --> 00:56:53,326
<i>- Okay, thank you.</i>
- Thank you.

1349
00:56:53,409 --> 00:56:55,120
Wait, how many are you?

1350
00:56:55,203 --> 00:56:56,746
THE BOSS IS BACK IN ACTION

1351
00:56:56,830 --> 00:56:59,415
Two people? Okay, see you later.

1352
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:01,334
<i>- Bye.</i>
<i>- Bye.</i>

1353
00:57:02,502 --> 00:57:04,963
Then they don't know about us, right?

1354
00:57:05,046 --> 00:57:07,006
- The guests don't know.
- Not yet.

1355
00:57:07,090 --> 00:57:10,135
- Right. They don't know about you guys.
- They don't.

1356
00:57:10,218 --> 00:57:12,512
You heard a different man's voice, right?

1357
00:57:12,595 --> 00:57:14,264
- Yes.
- Try to guess it.

1358
00:57:14,347 --> 00:57:17,183
I think he's an actor,
judging by the voice.

1359
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:19,102
- I'm so curious.
- I think he's an actor.

1360
00:57:22,147 --> 00:57:23,940
DAEGWALLYEONG YANGTTE RANCH

1361
00:57:24,983 --> 00:57:27,902
- Wow, they're so cute.
- So cute.

1362
00:57:27,986 --> 00:57:29,279
They're so cute.

1363
00:57:29,362 --> 00:57:30,363
So cute.

1364
00:57:30,447 --> 00:57:31,406
I'll take a photo too.

1365
00:57:31,990 --> 00:57:33,199
Two, three.

1366
00:57:35,326 --> 00:57:38,746
HEADING TO KIAN'S B&B WITH HIGH HOPES

1367
00:57:38,830 --> 00:57:41,458
We have to cook dinner every day.

1368
00:57:41,541 --> 00:57:43,418
I practiced cooking <i>okonomiyaki.</i>

1369
00:57:43,501 --> 00:57:45,211
- Really?
- A little.

1370
00:57:45,295 --> 00:57:46,212
That's amazing.

1371
00:57:46,296 --> 00:57:48,339
You must've been busy, but you did it.

1372
00:57:48,423 --> 00:57:50,675
ARRIVING AT THE GROCERY STORE
2:00 P.M.

1373
00:57:50,758 --> 00:57:51,593
Thank you.

1374
00:57:51,676 --> 00:57:53,136
Hello.

1375
00:57:55,096 --> 00:57:56,055
All right. Now…

1376
00:57:56,723 --> 00:57:59,476
- Zuha, the ingredients for <i>okonomiyaki.</i>
- Do I only do that?

1377
00:57:59,559 --> 00:58:00,602
KIAN & JUN-HO'S CART

1378
00:58:00,685 --> 00:58:04,063
MEAT, CANNED TUNA, RAMYEON, SNACKS

1379
00:58:04,147 --> 00:58:06,065
YEON-KOUNG'S CART
BANANAS

1380
00:58:06,149 --> 00:58:08,610
GREEN GRAPES, BEER FOR GUESTS(?)

1381
00:58:08,693 --> 00:58:10,695
PASTA

1382
00:58:11,988 --> 00:58:14,240
- Kazuha, you need help?
- Potatoes.

1383
00:58:14,324 --> 00:58:15,575
CONFUSED ZUHA

1384
00:58:16,075 --> 00:58:17,994
- Potatoes? Check there.
- Where are they?

1385
00:58:18,578 --> 00:58:19,621
SHE CAN'T FIND POTATOES

1386
00:58:19,704 --> 00:58:20,914
There are sweet potatoes here.

1387
00:58:22,624 --> 00:58:24,375
"Potato" is written here.

1388
00:58:25,710 --> 00:58:27,045
I can't believe you.

1389
00:58:28,004 --> 00:58:30,381
Kazuha. Look, it says "potato."

1390
00:58:31,674 --> 00:58:33,176
I'm not Korean.

1391
00:58:34,886 --> 00:58:37,430
OKONOMIYAKI INGREDIENTS
POTATOES

1392
00:58:37,514 --> 00:58:39,682
Do you know where the yams are?

1393
00:58:40,433 --> 00:58:41,476
ASKING AN EMPLOYEE

1394
00:58:41,559 --> 00:58:42,685
Do we have yams?

1395
00:58:42,769 --> 00:58:43,811
NO YAMS

1396
00:58:43,895 --> 00:58:45,813
- We don't have them. Yes.
- Really?

1397
00:58:47,065 --> 00:58:48,066
What do I do?

1398
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:50,610
I'm doomed.

1399
00:58:51,611 --> 00:58:52,737
Hello?

1400
00:58:54,322 --> 00:58:56,699
If there are no yams, what do I do?

1401
00:58:56,783 --> 00:58:58,701
ASKING HER MOM FOR HELP

1402
00:58:58,785 --> 00:58:59,827
Lotus roots? Okay.

1403
00:59:00,870 --> 00:59:02,956
BUYING LOTUS ROOTS INSTEAD

1404
00:59:03,748 --> 00:59:05,583
Starch? Okay.

1405
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:08,336
2ND ALTERNATIVE: STARCH

1406
00:59:09,420 --> 00:59:11,464
Korean is hard.

1407
00:59:13,299 --> 00:59:15,510
These are all starch.

1408
00:59:15,593 --> 00:59:17,095
- All of them?
- Yes, starch.

1409
00:59:17,178 --> 00:59:19,222
THE STARCH WAS CLOSER THAN SHE THOUGHT

1410
00:59:23,726 --> 00:59:25,144
THE PHONE RINGS AGAIN

1411
00:59:25,228 --> 00:59:26,271
More guests?

1412
00:59:28,523 --> 00:59:29,774
Hello?

1413
00:59:29,857 --> 00:59:31,276
- Hello?
<i>- Hi.</i>

1414
00:59:31,359 --> 00:59:32,735
More guests are coming.

1415
00:59:32,819 --> 00:59:34,320
<i>Kian's B&B…</i>

1416
00:59:34,404 --> 00:59:35,321
Yes.

1417
00:59:35,405 --> 00:59:37,949
<i>- We're guests for today.</i>
- This is bad.

1418
00:59:38,032 --> 00:59:39,492
How many are you?

1419
00:59:39,576 --> 00:59:40,868
Two people.

1420
00:59:40,952 --> 00:59:41,828
Two people.

1421
00:59:41,911 --> 00:59:44,163
- What do we do?
- We're in trouble.

1422
00:59:44,247 --> 00:59:47,250
I'll send you the address.

1423
00:59:47,333 --> 00:59:48,876
<i>- Okay.</i>
- Bye.

1424
00:59:48,960 --> 00:59:50,962
- How many are coming?
- Two.

1425
00:59:51,045 --> 00:59:52,547
- Two more. Four, then.
- Yes.

1426
00:59:53,131 --> 00:59:54,299
Two men and two women.

1427
00:59:54,382 --> 00:59:55,675
GUESTS ON THE 1ST DAY
4 PEOPLE

1428
01:00:02,181 --> 01:00:04,225
- It looks so small from here.
- Right.

1429
01:00:04,309 --> 01:00:05,977
- It looks small.
- Yes.

1430
01:00:06,060 --> 01:00:06,978
I'm scared.

1431
01:00:07,061 --> 01:00:09,731
3:00 P.M.

1432
01:00:09,814 --> 01:00:11,441
- Thank you.
- Sure.

1433
01:00:11,524 --> 01:00:12,734
Thank you.

1434
01:00:12,817 --> 01:00:14,902
Carry this. It's lighter.

1435
01:00:15,403 --> 01:00:17,739
- God! You said it was light.
- It's the lightest one.

1436
01:00:17,822 --> 01:00:19,157
You little punk.

1437
01:00:19,240 --> 01:00:20,241
You punk!

1438
01:00:20,867 --> 01:00:22,118
Gosh, it's heavy.

1439
01:00:23,494 --> 01:00:24,412
It's so far.

1440
01:00:27,707 --> 01:00:30,918
I think it's between 25 kg and 30 kg.

1441
01:00:33,546 --> 01:00:34,672
Is it heavy?

1442
01:00:35,256 --> 01:00:36,424
I'm good.

1443
01:00:37,925 --> 01:00:40,386
- Do we have to go back?
- Is there more?

1444
01:00:41,012 --> 01:00:42,805
ZUHA GOES TO HELP

1445
01:00:42,889 --> 01:00:43,973
Why?

1446
01:00:44,057 --> 01:00:45,308
Isn't there one more?

1447
01:00:45,391 --> 01:00:46,684
Is there more?

1448
01:00:47,602 --> 01:00:48,728
No.

1449
01:00:48,811 --> 01:00:50,313
Zuha, you just go back.

1450
01:00:50,938 --> 01:00:52,440
You won't be of much help.

1451
01:00:52,523 --> 01:00:54,525
You should come and organize them.

1452
01:00:55,777 --> 01:00:57,403
Why do you not worry about me?

1453
01:00:59,405 --> 01:01:01,157
They didn't tell me to come back.

1454
01:01:01,741 --> 01:01:03,076
I'm coming to help you.

1455
01:01:06,746 --> 01:01:08,706
You can't carry this alone.

1456
01:01:09,874 --> 01:01:11,501
One, two, three.

1457
01:01:11,584 --> 01:01:13,044
Are you okay?

1458
01:01:13,127 --> 01:01:15,088
Just come here, Zuha.

1459
01:01:22,345 --> 01:01:23,346
How is it?

1460
01:01:31,354 --> 01:01:33,064
JUN-HO HAS COME TO HELP

1461
01:01:33,147 --> 01:01:35,400
Carry this and the cabbage in there.

1462
01:01:37,068 --> 01:01:39,112
- Just two feel heavy, right?
- No.

1463
01:01:40,530 --> 01:01:42,115
Why isn't she opening the door?

1464
01:01:42,198 --> 01:01:44,158
- You have to do it.
- I'm so tired.

1465
01:01:44,242 --> 01:01:45,535
- Boss, should I carry it?
- What?

1466
01:01:46,119 --> 01:01:47,036
We're almost there.

1467
01:01:50,373 --> 01:01:51,708
Let's put it down here.

1468
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:08,057
I'll do it.

1469
01:02:08,891 --> 01:02:11,519
- How heavy are you?
- I'm heavier than I look.

1470
01:02:11,602 --> 01:02:12,812
Let me carry you.

1471
01:02:15,481 --> 01:02:16,691
YEON-KOUNG'S SO TALL

1472
01:02:16,774 --> 01:02:17,734
- Climb up.
- Wait.

1473
01:02:18,359 --> 01:02:19,318
Darn it!

1474
01:02:20,570 --> 01:02:22,530
THE SAME AS YEON-KOUNG'S HEIGHT

1475
01:02:22,613 --> 01:02:23,990
- She can't reach it.
- She can't.

1476
01:02:24,073 --> 01:02:25,450
NOT EVEN CLOSE

1477
01:02:25,533 --> 01:02:27,368
- She can't reach it.
- One, two, three.

1478
01:02:28,035 --> 01:02:29,746
- You can't?
- I can't.

1479
01:02:29,829 --> 01:02:30,705
We can't.

1480
01:02:31,831 --> 01:02:32,665
Let's do it.

1481
01:02:34,250 --> 01:02:35,710
Are you okay?

1482
01:02:36,377 --> 01:02:38,212
- Are you sure?
- This is the last time.

1483
01:02:38,296 --> 01:02:39,714
One, two, three.

1484
01:02:39,797 --> 01:02:41,716
Okay.

1485
01:02:42,425 --> 01:02:43,760
All right. Open.

1486
01:02:44,969 --> 01:02:45,970
Pull. It's open.

1487
01:02:46,512 --> 01:02:49,223
So why did you have to make it this way?

1488
01:02:49,307 --> 01:02:50,850
Hopes and romance.

1489
01:02:50,933 --> 01:02:53,019
Hopes and romance, and nothing else.

1490
01:02:53,102 --> 01:02:54,771
And nothing else?

1491
01:02:57,940 --> 01:02:59,358
This is not right.

1492
01:03:01,277 --> 01:03:03,529
We have to take it up to the second floor.

1493
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:09,619
IT'S LAUGHABLE

1494
01:03:09,702 --> 01:03:12,079
It's only fun when building it.

1495
01:03:12,622 --> 01:03:13,831
Only when I imagined it.

1496
01:03:14,415 --> 01:03:17,502
We can leave the snacks down here.

1497
01:03:17,585 --> 01:03:19,253
- Only vegetables.
- Yes.

1498
01:03:19,337 --> 01:03:21,339
SORTING BOXES FOR THE SINK AREA

1499
01:03:23,633 --> 01:03:24,967
Okay, it's done.

1500
01:03:28,763 --> 01:03:30,556
HIS COLD HAS GOTTEN WORSE

1501
01:03:37,438 --> 01:03:39,440
HE PUTS THE TISSUES IN

1502
01:03:40,775 --> 01:03:41,692
Okay.

1503
01:03:48,449 --> 01:03:50,910
Why did I build it like this?

1504
01:03:55,206 --> 01:03:57,166
I'll try pulling it
with the rope from here.

1505
01:03:57,250 --> 01:03:58,334
A ROPE?

1506
01:03:58,417 --> 01:04:01,420
<i>It'll be so inconvenient</i>
<i>if everyone has to climb up.</i>

1507
01:04:01,504 --> 01:04:03,339
Maybe we can use a rope.

1508
01:04:03,422 --> 01:04:05,716
Like a shoelace.

1509
01:04:05,800 --> 01:04:08,761
It'll be nice to lift things using that.

1510
01:04:10,429 --> 01:04:12,598
Should we try lifting them with this rope?

1511
01:04:13,516 --> 01:04:14,433
TIE IT TIGHTLY

1512
01:04:16,018 --> 01:04:17,270
- Can you lift it?
- Yes.

1513
01:04:17,353 --> 01:04:18,271
- All right.
- I'll pull.

1514
01:04:18,354 --> 01:04:19,355
One, two, three!

1515
01:04:20,147 --> 01:04:20,982
Wait.

1516
01:04:21,065 --> 01:04:22,108
One, two, three!

1517
01:04:22,859 --> 01:04:23,693
Wait.

1518
01:04:23,776 --> 01:04:26,153
KIAN'S PULLEY

1519
01:04:27,363 --> 01:04:28,197
Okay.

1520
01:04:28,698 --> 01:04:29,699
Can you lift it?

1521
01:04:30,324 --> 01:04:31,158
Can you?

1522
01:04:34,078 --> 01:04:35,413
He's doing it.

1523
01:04:37,874 --> 01:04:38,708
HE LIFTED IT UP

1524
01:04:40,960 --> 01:04:42,044
Okay.

1525
01:04:42,128 --> 01:04:43,170
Great.

1526
01:04:44,005 --> 01:04:45,006
This is exhausting.

1527
01:04:46,716 --> 01:04:48,843
Hey, take it with your hand.

1528
01:04:48,926 --> 01:04:51,053
- We should support the bottom.
- Right.

1529
01:04:53,723 --> 01:04:54,640
It's done.

1530
01:04:56,309 --> 01:04:57,894
Good work.

1531
01:05:00,855 --> 01:05:02,440
It's time for them to come.

1532
01:05:02,523 --> 01:05:04,233
3:30 P.M.

1533
01:05:04,317 --> 01:05:05,985
- It's all ready.
- What?

1534
01:05:06,736 --> 01:05:07,570
Is it?

1535
01:05:07,653 --> 01:05:09,697
- They can come.
- Okay.

1536
01:05:09,780 --> 01:05:11,157
- Soon.
- Hey, the door…

1537
01:05:11,240 --> 01:05:12,950
Should we have them open it?

1538
01:05:13,576 --> 01:05:17,204
GUESTS HAVE TO OPEN THE 5-M-TALL DOOR?

1539
01:05:17,288 --> 01:05:19,415
I want them to experience it.

1540
01:05:19,498 --> 01:05:22,126
If they don't know how to open it,
it won't be easy.

1541
01:05:23,252 --> 01:05:24,378
